From 48bda7fa2154417ba49d8ed5c9bf4ddb6b5ef00d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sjcsf <346224915+llsf2020@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/20] FreeChat: new messages without a push app

Two more ways to get notifications, offered next to UnifiedPush under
"Push notification provider":
- Periodic checks (the default without a UnifiedPush app): about every
  15 minutes a WorkManager job asks the homeserver's /notifications for
  unread notifications newer than the last check, and hands them to the
  push handler like pushed ones. No pusher is registered.
- Built-in connection: the app subscribes to a random up* topic of the
  ntfy on the user's own homeserver and registers it as the pusher, so
  it does what the ntfy app would. A specialUse foreground service with
  a silent notification keeps the JSON stream open, reconnects with a
  backoff or as soon as the network is back, and starts again after a
  reboot or an update.
MatrixClient.clientApiRequest generalises freechatRequest to any
client-server API path. The push loopback test is hidden for periodic
checks, which have no pusher.
